{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Pre-claim investigation 2026-10-31 (no claim, no code change): the full-SHA requirement is deliberate, not an accidental string compare. scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py _revision_matches requires len(inspected) == 40, and the originating commit 8025b323b2f (ticket 8b1c-c577-366b-47d5) added tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py::test_safe_submit_refuses_abbreviated_revision_prefix, which asserts that a prefix of the current revision is refused with exit 2. CONTRIBUTING.md §2e and AGENTS.md both document --revision <current-full-sha>. No rationale for the 40-character rule is recorded in that commit, its ticket, or the tracker/mempalace search. Accepting prefixes (this ticket's Change section) reverses a tested design; the alternative is to keep requiring the full SHA and replace the staleness wording with a length/format message. Work paused pending an operator decision between those two."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793470140687458001,"uuid":"e40c5ab3-ccb4-4367-bbf3-9810a6865dd7"}